nd) for command palettes, custom searchable popups, and paged hierarchical pickers."},"667":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-164","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#picker-choice","content":"Changing the trigger appearance does not change the component choice. Keep Select and Combobox as their own roots; build hierarchical path pickers from Popover + Command."},"668":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-165","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#picker-choice","content":"Do not wrap Select, Combobox, or custom Command pickers inside DropdownMenu to get a button trigger. Use DropdownMenu only when the popup rows are commands rather than a bound value."},"669":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-166","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#imports","content":"Replace package imports with local imports:"},"670":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-167","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#imports","content":"Compound components use named exports:"},"671":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-168","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Button no longer owns icons or loading state. Move icons and spinners into children, and mark them with data-icon=\"inline-start\" or data-icon=\"inline-end\"."},"672":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-169","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Replace isLoading with an explicit disabled button plus Spinner.\nInstall @vital-design/spinner if your app needs the shared spinner."},"673":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-170","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Icon-only buttons now use size variants instead of empty children or icon props:"},"674":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-171","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"Keep size=\"md\" or size=\"lg\" for buttons with labels. For filled label buttons, v1 keeps the v0 spacing contract: the icon side is 12px, and the non-icon side is 16px.\nIf you used earlier v1 draft size names, rename medium to md, large to lg, icon-medium to icon-md, and icon-large to icon-lg."},"675":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-172","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"The variant prop renamed filled to default. The new ghost variant is a transparent button with hover background — use it inside popovers, toolbars, and split-button menus (it backs the Popup Button pattern)."},"676":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-173","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#button","content":"The theme enum keeps alarm (filled red) and dangerous (white surface with red text) as distinct intents — alarm is only available on variant=\"default\". The dangerous theme renders bordered at size=\"md\" and shadow-elevated at size=\"lg\", mirroring the Figma \"Outlined\" guideline."},"677":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-174","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#text-input-value-changes","content":"Input is built on Base UI's input primitive. For controlled value\nupdates, prefer onValueChange; keep native onChange only when the\ncaller needs the DOM change event."},"678":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-175","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#invalid-form-controls","content":"V1-only isError props are removed from v2 form controls. Use aria-invalid on the actual control instead."},"679":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-176","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#invalid-form-controls","content":"When using Field, set invalid state on both the field wrapper and the control: Field data-invalid handles label/help text styling, while aria-invalid on the actual control handles control semantics and the visible border."},"680":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-177","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#switch","content":"Switch now follows the Base UI callback name. Replace onChange with onCheckedChange; root props such as defaultChecked, name, value, disabled, and aria-invalid pass through."},"681":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-178","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Install @vital-design/label when a migrated screen has standalone text associated with a form control."},"682":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-179","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Use Label for visible field labels that point at Input, InputGroupInput, Textarea, or PasswordInput with htmlFor."},"683":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide-180","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/migration-guide#label","content":"Do not hide low-level label comp