theme, size, className, and contentClassName like\nButton, plus every <a> attribute and render. It has no disabled prop,\nbecause links cannot be disabled. Render plain text or a Button instead. The\nroot uses data-slot=\"link-button\" and the content wrapper uses\ndata-slot=\"link-button-content\"."},"1246":{"id":"/docs/components/button-90","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#laying-out-the-content","content":"Button wraps its children in a span[data-slot=\"button-content\"] that centres\nthe icon and label and keeps them on one line. Since that span is the button's\nonly child, flex utilities written on the button itself have nothing to\ndistribute — use contentClassName to reach the wrapper instead of selecting\ninto it with [&>span]:*."},"1247":{"id":"/docs/components/button-91","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#laying-out-the-content","content":"Colour, size, radius, and hover states stay owned by the theme — passing those\nthrough className will not override the variant. The button also sets\noverflow-hidden for its hover overlay, so a child positioned outside the\nbutton box (a notification badge at -top-1 -right-1) needs\nclassName=\"overflow-visible\" on the button."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"page","content":"Calendar","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar"},"1249":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar","content":"Date picker calendar built on react-day-picker. Single, range, and multi-select modes with full classNames and components overrides."},"1250":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#preview","content":"Preview"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/calen